# Token spend — orchestrate high, execute cheap

Use a **top-tier model for orchestration** (plan, decide, review, synthesize). Use **efficient smaller models for execution** via the Task tool. Do not burn the expensive parent on long mechanical work a cheaper subagent can do.

## Model routing (when available)

| Work | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Orchestration, ambiguous design calls, final synthesis | Parent / top-tier (`inherit` only when the subtask itself needs that judgment) |
| Fast mechanical edit, boilerplate, search-and-edit, shell | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| Medium exploration / multi-file implementation | `cursor-grok-4.6-medium` or `gpt-5.6-sol-medium` |

## How to run it

- Orchestrator owns: intent, acceptance criteria, prioritization, conflict resolution, user-facing answer.
- Execution agents get a **self-contained** prompt with all needed context — do not dump full transcripts into every subagent.
- Prefer **parallel** Task calls for independent work.
- Goal: maximize quality of decisions; minimize tokens on repetitive execution.
